~ start
Lisa Stone: Captain... what did Bob die for?
You: He betrayed the crew. He betrayed me.
Lisa Stone: All he wanted was to see his home again, to see his family. Why not just drop him off on an island? Why kill him?
You: He could've left whenever he wanted, but he chose violence when he chose to lead the mutiny. We're pirates. We're violent and uncivilized. The one thing we should have is loyalty. And Bob had none.
Lisa Stone: I know we're pirates. I know we've killed. But how am I supposed to have loyalty to the crew when we be killing our own?
You: I do what I can to keep this crew together. But to do that I need the crew to be loyal to me. 
Lisa Stone: In your fight for loyalty, I fear you be destroying it.
=> END